== What was measured

The primary metric is the first degree where the homogeneous quotient is zero for the ideal generated by the original individual highest forms, including Boolean squares. Affine row combinations were not taken before forming the highest forms. The result is a degree-of-regularity census for the frozen equation systems and factor-base inputs. It is not first-fall degree, last-fall degree, affine solving degree, or a timed attack-cost measurement.

The frozen panel contains 28 unique inputs: two families x seven m values x natural/planted target. The inputs and source files are SHA-256 bound in `inputs.manifest.json` and retain their existing S3 object URIs. The selected factor-base manifest is `r=38`, with hashes recorded per case. No factor-base points or targets were sampled during this run.

